WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.520
This is the example we left at in the previous video.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.860
If we drop a piece of Balsa wood and a metal pin

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.140
of the same mass into the water. What will happen?

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.640
Will both of them float or will both of them sink?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.280
Or one stays afloat and one sinks?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.920
Just by intuition we can say that the wooden block will float

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.920
and the metal pin will sink.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.760
But if they're of the same mass, why does that happen?

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.140
Shouldn't both float because of the buoyant force?

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.040
This happens because of the difference in the densities. But what's density?

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.200
Look at these two parking lots of the same size.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.080
One has three cars and the other has many cars.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.600
Which one is more dense? This one, correct? Yes!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.360
Now look at these two forests. Which one is more dense with trees?

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.660
Clearly its this one.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.660
So in the same given amount of space,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.060
if there are more things, we say that its denser.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.880
Density is simply the measure of how compact

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.560
the mass in a substance or object is..

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.300
If we have to go by its scientific definition.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.800
We would say that it's mass per unit volume.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.780
In short, it tells us how much mass exists in a given volume.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.420
The unit of density is "kilogram per meter cubed".

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.940
Mass is in kilograms and volume in meter cubed.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.360
Coming back to our example. Why did the wood float and the pin sink?

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.320
The wood floated on water because the density of the wood

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.780
is lesser than the density of water.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.760
Hence the upthrust of water on the wood

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.060
is greater than the weight of the wood. Hence it floated.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.060
But the density of a metal pin is more than the density of water.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.980
Though it looks tiny.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.920
There's more mass per unit volume within it as compared to water.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.740
Hence the upthrust of water on the pin is less than the weight of the pin.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.040
So what can we conclude?

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:12.520
If the density of an object is lesser than the density of the liquid,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.120
then it will float.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.260
And if the density of an object is more than the density of the liquid then,

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.260
it will sink.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.480
We will understand the Archimedes principle in the next video.

